            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_UI_CLOSE">
                <English>Close</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_UI_SUPPLY_LINE">
                <English>Supply: %1</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_UI_NO_CATALOG">
                <English>The build list is still being made. Try again in a moment.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_UI_FORTIFICATION">
                <English>Fortification</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_UI_SUPPLY_ITEM">
                <English>Supply</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_UI_COST">
                <English>Costs %1 supply</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_REFUSED_NOFOB">
                <English>That FOB is gone.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_REFUSED_DAMAGED_BUILD">
                <English>Nothing can be built at a damaged FOB until it's repaired.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_REFUSED_NOTBUILDABLE">
                <English>That can't be built at a FOB.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_REFUSED_TIER">
                <English>The FOB has to reach tier %1 to build that.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_REFUSED_SUPPLY">
                <English>That needs %1 supply and the FOB has %2.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_REFUSED_NOTBUILT">
                <English>That wasn't built at a FOB.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_BUILT">
                <English>%1 built for %2 supply.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_RECYCLED">
                <English>%1 recycled: %2 supply back.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_UI_STATICS">
                <English>Statics</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_UI_STATIC_ITEM">
                <English>Static weapon, crewed by your side</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_REFUSED_STATIC_SIDE">
                <English>Your side can only build the static weapons and vehicles its own forces use.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_REFUSED_STATIC_PROFILES">
                <English>Static weapons and vehicles need the Virtual AI System module in the mission.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_ALERT_RADIUS">
                <English>Alert Radius</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_ALERT_RADIUS_COMMENT">
                <English>How close, in metres, the enemy has to come before the FOB's side hears on the radio that it's under threat.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_CAPTURE_RADIUS">
                <English>Capture Radius</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_CAPTURE_RADIUS_COMMENT">
                <English>Enemy soldiers inside this many metres, with none of the FOB's side, start taking the FOB. Enemy players alone don't take it.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_CAPTURE_TIME">
                <English>Capture Time</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_CAPTURE_TIME_COMMENT">
                <English>Seconds the enemy has to hold the FOB, unopposed, before it becomes theirs. Any defender in the capture radius starts the count again.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_REPAIR_TIME">
                <English>Repair Time</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_REPAIR_TIME_COMMENT">
                <English>Seconds a FOB with a destroyed headquarters has before it's lost for good, unless repaired. The count stops while an engineer of its side is within 25 m.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_REPAIR_COST">
                <English>Repair Cost</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_REPAIR_COST_COMMENT">
                <English>Supply to repair a destroyed headquarters at tier 1; one and a half times at tier 2, twice at tier 3. A quarter off with an engineer present.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_ACTION_REPAIR">
                <English>Repair FOB</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_REPAIRED">
                <English>%1 repaired for %2 supply.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_REFUSED_NOT_DAMAGED">
                <English>That FOB doesn't need repairing.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_CRATE_AMOUNT">
                <English>Supply Crate Amount</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_CRATE_AMOUNT_COMMENT">
                <English>How much supply a crate from a Field HQ holds. In Force Pool mode the faction's pool pays this for the crate.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_KIT_COST">
                <English>FOB Kit Cost</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_KIT_COST_COMMENT">
                <English>What a FOB kit from a Field HQ costs the faction's force pool, in Force Pool mode only; free otherwise. Sync any object to the module to make it a Field HQ.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_TIER2_COST">
                <English>Tier 2 Cost</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_TIER3_COST">
                <English>Tier 3 Cost</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_TIER_COST_COMMENT">
                <English>Supply to upgrade a FOB to this tier. Tier 2 can hold more supply and builds towers, machine guns and grenade launchers; tier 3 holds the most, builds mortars, AT and AA launchers and vehicles, and can be a respawn point.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_RESPAWN_OFF">
                <English>Off</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_RESPAWN_T1">
                <English>From tier 1 (as soon as it's deployed)</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_RESPAWN_T2">
                <English>From tier 2</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_RESPAWN_T3">
                <English>From tier 3</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_RESPAWN">
                <English>Respawn Point</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_RESPAWN_COMMENT">
                <English>From which tier a FOB is a respawn point for its side, while its headquarters stands. Off: never. Needs a respawn type in the mission that offers respawn positions.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_ACTION_UPGRADE">
                <English>Upgrade FOB</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_ACTION_UNLOAD">
                <English>Unload Supplies</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_ACTION_HQ_KIT">
                <English>Request FOB Kit</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_ACTION_HQ_CRATE">
                <English>Request Supply Crate</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_UI_TIER_SHORT">
                <English>tier %1</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_UI_TIER_NEEDED">
                <English>Needs a tier %1 FOB</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_REFUSED_NOTCRATE">
                <English>That isn't a supply crate.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_REFUSED_FULL">
                <English>The FOB can't hold any more supply.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_REFUSED_TOPTIER">
                <English>The FOB is already at tier 3.</English>
            </Key>
            <Key ID="STR_ALIVE_FOB_REFUSED_POOL">
                <English>Your side's force pool doesn't have the %1 it costs.</English>
